    {
      "id": "02150307-632d-46e5-bdb7-e2c128a6e8e0",
      "name": "Overview - Payment Monitoring & Recovery",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1056,
        272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 900,
        "height": 546,
        "content": "# Payment Monitoring & Recovery\n\nReusable payment-recovery automation for finance teams. It reconciles invoice and payment records, sends staged reminders, routes sensitive escalations through email approval, and reports outcomes.\n\n**Flow**\n1. Read the invoice register and latest payment records.\n2. Reconcile balances and calculate overdue age and risk.\n3. Send standard reminders or queue sensitive cases for approval.\n4. Record the finance decision; send the final notice only when approved.\n5. Send the daily finance summary and capture workflow failures.\n\n**Before activation**\n- Replace `YOUR_FINANCE_SPREADSHEET_ID`; create `Invoices`, `Payments`, `Approval Queue`, and `Reminder Audit Log`.\n- Confirm invoice fields: `Invoice_ID`, `Email`, `Due_Date`, `Amount`, `Amount_Paid`, `Payment_Status`, `Dispute_Status`, `Last_Reminder_Date`, `Reminder_Count`, `Dunning_Stage`, `Approval_Status`, and `Approval_Decision_Date`.\n- Connect Google Sheets and Gmail credentials; replace `finance-approver@example.com` and use test recipients first.\n- Review thresholds and instance timezone. Test reminder, approval, rejection, summary, and error paths with controlled data.\n\nKeep inactive until configuration and supervised tests are complete."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "41c9cffb-9347-414c-a91b-0fd0dbc2fe4a",
      "name": "Section - Monitoring and Dunning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -16,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1072,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## 1. Monitoring and dunning\n\n**Inputs:** `Invoices` and `Payments` tabs in the finance workbook.\n\n**Policy:** Recalculate outstanding balances using recent payment rows. Skip paid, settled, cancelled, disputed, invalid, or recently reminded invoices. Apply first/second/final reminder stages and a risk score. Final-stage or high-risk cases enter the approval path; ordinary cases receive a standard reminder.\n\n**Outputs:** The standard-reminder path updates the invoice state and appends a sent outcome to `Reminder Audit Log`. The sensitive-case path creates an approval-queue record and waits for finance approval. A three-day quiet period helps avoid repeat reminders."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
